Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] dt-bindings: iommu: apple,sart: Add t6050 (SARTv4)
 compatible

The SART found on the Apple M5 Pro/Max SoC (t6050; ADT compatible
"sart,coastguard", ADT property sart-version = 4) keeps the SARTv3 entry
format but moves the PADDR array from 0x40 to 0x60 and the SIZE array
from 0x80 to 0xc0.  A driver for SARTv3 would program the wrong
registers, so the new compatible has no fallback.

Evidence: ADT of a Mac17,6 (J716c) captured with the workspace's
sanitizing extractor (sart-version = 4); register layout from m1n1
src/sart.c (commit 9bfdf8aeca30 "sart: add SARTv4 support", MIT-licensed
at tag v1.9.9).

NOT FOR UPSTREAM SUBMISSION: AI-generated local research draft (Asahi
Linux generative-AI policy).  No Signed-off-by on purpose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,sart.yaml | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,sart.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,sart.yaml
index 8fd77757..5f742085 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,sart.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,sart.yaml
@@ -26,6 +26,10 @@ description:
   SART3, first seen in M1 Pro/Max, extends both the address space and filter
   entry size to 42 bit.
 
+  SART4, first seen in M5 Pro/Max, keeps the SART3 entry format but moves the
+  physical address and size register arrays, so it is not compatible with
+  SART3.
+
 properties:
   compatible:
     oneOf:
@@ -37,6 +41,7 @@ properties:
           - const: apple,t6000-sart
       - enum:
           - apple,t6000-sart
+          - apple,t6050-sart
           - apple,t8015-sart
           - apple,t8103-sart
 

